  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: Entrepreneurial ecosystem connect week</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is aimed at organising the Orange Corners Entrepreneurship Festival in Burundi, a three-day event combining a conference, exhibition-sale, graduation ceremonies, and a public cultural event. The festival will showcase the accomplishments of Orange Corners entrepreneurs from the Orange Corners Incubation and Acceleration Component (OCIAC) and Orange Corners Innovation Fund (OCIF), celebrate the graduation of cohorts 3 and 4, and announce the winners of the next OCIF cohort. By bringing together entrepreneurs, Entrepreneurial support organizations (ESOs), donors, investors, government representatives, and the wider public, the event will foster collaboration, highlight innovation, and increase the visibility of youth entrepreneurship in Burundi. The festival will serve as a catalyst for entrepreneurial growth, market access, and ecosystem strengthening in the country.</narrative>
  </description>
